# Example: the backup loop (the `backup` compose profile), with a routine backup outside crunch
# week. A fragment layered over deploy/oss/.env.example after env/minimal.env. Without
# ATLAS_BACKUP_SCHEDULE the loop acts only during a crunch week whose backup policy is once,
# hourly or daily (crunch/crunch-week.yaml shows one); the per_deploy policy is run by the
# pipeline instead. Every backup is restored into a temporary database and counted before it is
# kept. Restore one with `atlas-admin backup restore latest` (and undo that with
# `atlas-admin backup rollback`), as docs/oss/guides/operations.md describes.

# Start the backup profile with every `docker compose up` (no --profile flag needed).
# To run the gateway profile too, list both: COMPOSE_PROFILES=gateway,backup
COMPOSE_PROFILES=backup
# A routine backup outside crunch week: off (the default), hourly, daily or weekly. A crunch
# policy is asked first; the routine backup is taken only when the crunch took none.
ATLAS_BACKUP_SCHEDULE=daily
# How many routine backups to keep (1-1000, default 7). Manual, per-deploy and crunch backups
# are never deleted by it.
ATLAS_BACKUP_KEEP=7
# Backups land in the `atlas-backups` volume. To keep them in a host directory instead (so they
# can be copied off this host), create it writable by the container's group 0 first
# (`sudo install -d -m 0770 -g 0 /srv/atlas-backups`), then set:
# ATLAS_BACKUP_HOST_DIR=/srv/atlas-backups
